      "field_path": "fertilizer.notes_seasoned",
      "our_prose": "Nasturtium is the rare flower that should not be fed: it blooms best in lean soil, and added nitrogen or fertilizer drives leafy growth at the expense of flowers. On genuinely poor or sandy soil, at most one light, low-nitrogen feeding can help, but in average soil skip fertilizer entirely. Over-feeding is the most common reason a healthy-looking nasturtium refuses to bloom.",
